      "short": "Logged in",
      "chapter": "setup",
      "title": "Logged in is not allowed",
      "body": [
        "<b>Ledgerly</b> hosts invoices for thousands of small firms in one database. Login works well — every request carries a signed token saying who the caller is. That's authentication.",
        "<span class=\"term\">Authorization</span> is the next question: <i>may this person do this to this thing?</i> Ledgerly's API mostly relies on the app — it only shows you your own invoices, and hides buttons you shouldn't press."
      ],
