    {
      "short": "IDOR",
      "chapter": "problem",
      "title": "Just change the number",
      "body": [
        "Bo, at another firm, opens his invoice <code>/invoices/2210</code>, edits the URL to <code>1042</code> — and gets Pinecraft's invoice, bank details and all. The API checked Bo was logged in, not that the invoice was his.",
        "This is an <span class=\"term\">IDOR</span>, one of the most common serious web bugs. Hiding links in the UI does nothing: anyone can send any request with any ID."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "warn",
        "text": "The client is the attacker's computer. Every rule the UI enforces must be enforced again on the server."
      },
      "changes": [
        "~ Bo requests an invoice ID he doesn't own",
        "~ API returns it"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "exposed": "yes",
        "checks": "token only",
        "privilege": "—"
