    {
      "short": "Central policy",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "One policy, many enforcers",
      "body": [
        "Ledgerly moves the rules into a <span class=\"term\">policy engine</span>. Services stay the <b>enforcement points</b>: on each request they ask \"may user X do action Y on resource Z?\" and obey the answer. The decisions come from one place.",
        "Policies live as code: reviewed, versioned, unit-tested and logged on every decision. A rule change ships once and applies everywhere. Keep the engine close — usually a sidecar or library with cached policy — so the check costs microseconds, not a network round-trip."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Central policy engine",
        "~ All three services ask before acting",
        "+ Every decision logged for audit"
      ],
