    {
      "short": "Least priv.",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "Least privilege between services",
      "body": [
        "Apply <span class=\"term\">least privilege</span>: each service gets its own identity and only the access its job needs. Reports gets a read-only role on a reporting view — nothing else.",
        "Services prove who they are with mutual TLS or short-lived workload tokens, and the Invoices API authorizes by caller identity too. Acting for a user, Reports passes the user's context so tenant rules still apply."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Assume something will be compromised. Design so that when it is, it can reach as little as possible."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ Per-service identities",
        "~ Reports: read-only view only",
        "- Shared admin credentials"
      ],
